# Make checkouts and "Download ZIP" behave exactly like the released package.
#
# The reason this file exists: cmd.exe re-reads a *running* batch file from
# disk while it executes, and it assumes CRLF. A bare LF makes it resume in the
# middle of a line and try to run word fragments as commands, which shows up as
# a screenful of  'ery' is not recognized as an internal or external command.
# Without these rules git would store the .bat files as LF and anybody who
# grabbed the source zip would get broken launchers.
#
# The .exe that ships in the GitHub Release is an uploaded binary and is NOT
# affected by any of this - only the repository contents are.

* text=auto

# cmd.exe launchers: must stay CRLF, always.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Files printed with "type" under chcp 65001, or opened in Notepad.
*.txt text eol=crlf

# C# / PowerShell sources are UTF-8 *with* BOM on purpose: csc.exe and
# PowerShell 5.1 decode them as ANSI/GBK when the BOM is missing, which turns
# every Chinese string into garbage (and can even be a syntax error).
# git preserves the BOM byte-for-byte; these rules only pin the line endings.
*.cs  text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch, never diff, never "normalise".
*.exe binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
